@startuml
title Kubernetes Pod Communication via VLAN Interfaces

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #333333
  ActorBorderColor #333333
  LifeLineBorderColor #666666
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontSize 12
}

' Define participants with network interfaces
participant "Pod A" as PodA
participant "Pod A net1\n2.1.0.10/24" as PodA_net1
participant "Pod A net2\n2.1.1.10/24" as PodA_net2
participant "VLAN 2000 Bridge" as VLAN2000
participant "VLAN 2001 Bridge" as VLAN2001
participant "Pod B net1\n2.1.0.11/24" as PodB_net1
participant "Pod B net2\n2.1.1.11/24" as PodB_net2
participant "Pod B" as PodB

' Communication via VLAN 2000 (net1 interfaces)
note over PodA, VLAN2000: <b>VLAN 2000 Communication via net1</b>\nSubnet: 2.1.0.0/24
PodA -> PodA_net1 : 1. Send packet to 2.1.0.11
PodA_net1 -> VLAN2000 : 2. Forward via net1
VLAN2000 -> PodB_net1 : 3. Deliver to Pod B net1
PodB_net1 -> PodB : 4. Receive packet

PodB -> PodB_net1 : 5. Send reply to 2.1.0.10
PodB_net1 -> VLAN2000 : 6. Forward via net1
VLAN2000 -> PodA_net1 : 7. Deliver to Pod A net1
PodA_net1 -> PodA : 8. Receive reply
note over PodA, PodB: <b>VLAN 2000 communication complete</b>

' Communication via VLAN 2001 (net2 interfaces)
note over PodA, VLAN2001: <b>VLAN 2001 Communication via net2</b>\nSubnet: 2.1.1.0/24
PodA -> PodA_net2 : 9. Send packet to 2.1.1.11
PodA_net2 -> VLAN2001 : 10. Forward via net2
VLAN2001 -> PodB_net2 : 11. Deliver to Pod B net2
PodB_net2 -> PodB : 12. Receive packet

PodB -> PodB_net2 : 13. Send reply to 2.1.1.10
PodB_net2 -> VLAN2001 : 14. Forward via net2
VLAN2001 -> PodA_net2 : 15. Deliver to Pod A net2
PodA_net2 -> PodA : 16. Receive reply
note over PodA, PodB: <b>VLAN 2001 communication complete</b>

' Summary
note over PodA, PodB
<b>Summary:</b>
- Pod A uses net1 (2.1.0.10) for VLAN 2000
- Pod A uses net2 (2.1.1.10) for VLAN 2001
- Pod B uses net1 (2.1.0.11) for VLAN 2000
- Pod B uses net2 (2.1.1.11) for VLAN 2001
- Each VLAN is isolated at Layer 2
- No cross-VLAN routing between interfaces
end note

@enduml
